[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/441882030","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/62#issuecomment-441882030","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/62","id":441882030,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTg4MjAzMA==","user":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2012-07-28T11:30:35Z","updated_at":"2018-11-27T03:06:32Z","body":"**Michael Bayer ([@zzzeek](https://github.com/zzzeek)) wrote:**\n\nthis seems like user error, \"type_\" means you want to change the type of the column to \"boolean\".   If you want to change just nullability, you send the type along using \"existing_type\".   \"existing_type\" is of course only needed because DB's like MSSQL and MySQL don't have proper ALTER commands.\n\nHowever, I tried out \"existing_type\" and *that* seems to have a bug, in that it wants to *drop* the constraint.    So the logic to drop/create constraints given types is refined in [[https://bitbucket.org/zzzeek/alembic/changeset/50c7551d280fdaa099f15427b1627940181594f8|50c7551d280fdaa099f15427b1627940181594f8]] to include that the constraint is dropped only if existing_type *and* type_ is given, and additionally no constraints are impacted at all on dialects that don't need these constraints such as postgresql.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/441882030/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/441882031","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/62#issuecomment-441882031","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/62","id":441882031,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTg4MjAzMQ==","user":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avat